I am on the road to winning the game, halfway up through hell, and
wonder if it's worth my while to take some risks fighting the demon
lords along the way.  Right now I'm outside the lair of Orcus trying to
decide what to do.  So...

- I assume from reading the description of Orcus that he's got a wand of
death.  Will he really use it on me?  Or touch of death?  (This is after
my gray dragon scale mail went up in smoke against a black dragon.)

- Is there some approximate ranking of how powerful the different demon
lords are?  From doing some summoning with a ring of conflict on, it
seems like Yeenoghu is pretty powerful (moreso than Juiblex anyway :-).
I thought Demogorgon would be pretty wimpy -- I did manage to kill him,
but only after using up my amulet of life saving (and me with 164 HP!).
Where does Orcus rank?  Dispater?  I'm sure I've beaten up some of these
guys in previous games, but can't remember who.

- Are there any demon lords that pose no threat as long as I have a
unicorn horn?

- When I find lower levels of hell with nothing in the middle, is that
because I've previously summoned the lord who would normally be there?
Is it a good strategy to summon all the possible demon lords before
going to hell?

Mild spoiler:  if you want to get rid of something powerful in a temple,
or maybe something pesky like a temple priest, summon a demon lord while
wearing a ring of conflict.  (Never tried to leash one though, hmmm.)

